      "type": "text",
      "text": "I've marked this run as UNKNOWN and asked for a human to step in. The growth stage needs an exhaust oxygen reading to confirm the tube atmosphere, and this furnace doesn't have that sensor.\n\n- **Everything else looks normal:** temperature followed the ramp closely. It overshot by 10.5 °C when growth started, then settled at 750 ± 1 °C. Pressure held at about 760.5 Torr, which points away from a leak or blockage. Argon flow matched its setpoints of 200 and then 100 sccm, and heater power stayed steady at 44–46%.\n- **What's still unknown:** normal pressure and flow don't show the atmosphere was oxygen-free. So I can't call execution normal or anomalous.\n- **Growth results:** the sample hasn't been characterized yet.\n\nTo settle it, someone needs another way to check the atmosphere, such as an external leak check or looking for signs of oxidation. They also need to decide whether this run can count as evidence about the recipe once the sample is characterized."
     }
